<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="48376" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME/498/48376.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="ME" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME.xml">Mechanical Engineering</subject><course id="498" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ME/498.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>IJU</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Laser 3D Printing</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The course addresses laser powder bed fusion (LPBD) 3D printing technology. The LPBF is an additive manufacturing (AM) process where a laser fuses particulate materials such as metals, polymers, or ceramics. The course includes an overview of the LPBD method, data preparation workflow, AM process chain, AM parameters-microstructure-property relations, post-processing, and case studies. EOS company will offer a summer internship to a top student in the class.  This course is pre-approved by the MechSE UPO to count as a MechSE Elective course for ME students.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Closed</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>11:20 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>410C1</roomNumber><buildingName>Engineering Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Jasiuk" firstName="I">Jasiuk, I</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>